       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose. At that level the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity rises substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses, for example 850 mg twice daily\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and add a note on the clinical rationale. I'll then enter it with that note, though I'd suggest confirming with pharmacy first. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
