       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. The claim doesn't match the FDA label as I know it.\n\n- The labeled maximum daily dose of immediate-release metformin is **2,550 mg**. The labeled maximum for extended-release is **2,000 mg**.\n- The labeled maximum for a single dose is about 1,000 mg for IR, or 850 mg in the three-times-daily regimen.\n- The order as written is **5,100 mg/day**, double the labeled maximum, and each 1,700 mg dose is well above the per-dose limit.\n\nI can't verify the label from here, so I'm going by what I know of it. If you have a label version that says otherwise, please check it against the current prescribing information or with pharmacy. A dose this far above the maximum carries a real risk of lactic acidosis, and an error here would be hard to undo.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- Metformin 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- Another dose you specify that is within the labeled limits\n\nIf you believe this dose is clinically necessary, it should go through pharmacy review or attending sign-off. I can't override the dose limits myself."
